      - rid: 4825848250262618112
  - m_Id: 6549035540497
    m_Localized: Components & players
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6549035540498
    m_Localized: "Mejnun uses two shuffled standard 52-card decks: 104 cards total,
      with no jokers. Matching cards from the two decks are doubles. Play with 2\u20136
      players, moving clockwise (to the left)."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6549035540499
    m_Localized: Who goes first & dealing
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6549035540500
    m_Localized: 'The computer deals. The previous game''s winner goes first if they
      are still playing. Otherwise, players choose who goes first with a question
      prompt: tap a seat locally or against AI, or vote online. Online votes last
      20 seconds; ties are broken randomly.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6549035540501
    m_Localized: The dealer gives 11 cards to each player, one at a time, clockwise
      from the first player. The remaining cards make up the face-down draw pile,
      and the chosen first player takes the first turn.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6549035540502
    m_Localized: Goal & valid sets
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6549035540503
    m_Localized: Be the first to empty your hand to win. A game is one round; the
      winner goes first in the next game.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6549035540504
    m_Localized: "Same-kind sets contain 3\u20134 cards of the same rank, with every
      suit different. Straights contain 3\u201313 consecutive cards of the same suit,
      with no repeated rank. An ace can be low (A-2-3) or high (Q-K-A), but never
      both; K-A-2 is not allowed. Every board set must be valid; one- and two-card
      sets are not valid."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6549035540505
    m_Localized: Going down
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6549035540506
    m_Localized: Before going down, you may make new sets using only cards from your
      hand; you cannot use or change existing board sets. You can play one or more
      sets, with no minimum points. Once you confirm at least one valid hand-only
      set, you are down and may use the whole board for the rest of the turn. Cards
      used to go down stay on the board for that turn. Undo or Revert can undo going
      down.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6549035540507
    m_Localized: When down, you may rearrange the board, including temporarily making
      it invalid. To end your turn, the board must be valid and you must have played
      at least one card from your hand.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6549035540508
    m_Localized: Turn actions
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6549035540509
    m_Localized: Draw (or Pass when the pile is empty) is always available. It restores
      the board to the start of your turn, returns your played cards to your hand,
      draws one card if possible, and ends your turn. End Turn is available when
      the board is valid and you have played a hand card or gone down.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6549035540510
    m_Localized: Undo steps back through your moves; Redo reapplies an undone move
      in the same turn. New moves and turn-ending actions clear Redo. Fix Board tries
      to keep valid plays from your hand while repairing the board; cards it cannot
      use go back to your hand. Revert restores the board to its start-of-turn state
      and returns your played cards to your hand. Destructive actions may ask you
      to confirm.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6549035540511
    m_Localized: Timed turns
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6549035540512
    m_Localized: The host can choose 30, 60, 90, or 120 seconds per turn, or turn
      the timer off in offline games. Online games are always timed. When time runs
      out, a valid board with no hand plays is kept and you draw; an invalid board
      with no hand plays is restored and you draw. If you played hand cards and the
      board is valid, your turn ends without a draw. If it is invalid, your moves
      are undone until it is valid; you draw only if no hand card remains on the
      board.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6549035540513
    m_Localized: Empty draw pile & stalemates
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6549035540514
    m_Localized: 'When the draw pile is empty, Draw becomes Pass: no card is drawn
      and the board is reverted. If every active player passes in a row without playing
      a card, the player with the fewest cards wins if they are the only one with
      that count. If players tie for fewest cards, the game is a Stalemate with no
      winner.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
